<title>SOUTH KOREA: Hyundai Corp '96 net rises 3.4 pct.</title>
<headline>Hyundai Corp '96 net rises 3.4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31</p>
<p>(in billion won unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (won)			1,400 (gain) vs 1,800 (gain)</p>
<p>    Net				 12.3 (gain) vs 11.9 (gain)</p>
<p>    Turnover			     20,552.8 vs 16,742.3</p>
<p>    Loss/profit before tax	15.3 (gain) vs 15.2 (gain)</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries		0.16 (loss) vs 0.018 (gain)</p>
<p>Dividend Register Dec 31</p>
<p>NOTE - Hyundai Corp, a unit of the Hyundai Group, is one of South Korea's leading trading companies. The company's share capital increased by 3.3 million shares to 9.8 million shares at the end of 1996. A company spokesman said the rise was due to rights issues and dividends.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5645</p>
</text>
